.TH SETSOCKOPT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
setsockopt \- set a socket option
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.B int setsockopt(int descriptor, int level, int option, const void* value, socklen_t length);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets an option at SOL_SOCKET or a protocol level. Value and length must match
the option's Linux data type. The header defines common SO_* options and
struct linger; timeout options use the Linux timeval layout.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getsockopt (3crunch),
.BR setsockopt (2)
